{title: My Jesus, I Love Thee}
{artist: William R. Featherstone / Adoniram J. Gordon}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative, Response}
{key: F}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
My [F]Jesus, I [Bb]love Thee, I [F]know Thou art [C7]mine
For [F]Thee all the [Bb]follies of [F]sin I re[C7]sign
My [F]gracious Re[Dm]deemer, my [Gm]Saviour art [C7]Thou
If [F]ever I [Bb]loved Thee, my [F]Jesus, 'tis [C7]now [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [F]love Thee be[Bb]cause Thou hast [F]first loved [C7]me
And [F]purchased my [Bb]pardon on [F]Calvary's [C7]tree
I [F]love Thee for [Dm]wearing the [Gm]thorns on Thy [C7]brow
If [F]ever I [Bb]loved Thee, my [F]Jesus, 'tis [C7]now [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I'll [F]love Thee in [Bb]life, I will [F]love Thee in [C7]death
And [F]praise Thee as [Bb]long as Thou [F]lendest me [C7]breath
And [F]say when the [Dm]death-dew lies [Gm]cold on my [C7]brow
If [F]ever I [Bb]loved Thee, my [F]Jesus, 'tis [C7]now [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
In [F]mansions of [Bb]glory and [F]endless de[C7]light
I'll [F]ever a[Bb]dore Thee in [F]heaven so [C7]bright
I'll [F]sing with the [Dm]glittering [Gm]crown on my [C7]brow
If [F]ever I [Bb]loved Thee, my [F]Jesus, 'tis [C7]now [F]
{end_of_verse}
